# examples/lazyssh is a separate, independent project (its own go.mod,
# README, CI) — linked here as a git submodule rather than copied in,
# so it stays in sync with its own repo instead of drifting.
#
# POPULATING IT — a plain `git clone` of bubble-ssh leaves examples/lazyssh
# EMPTY. Either clone with submodules from the start:
#
#	git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/muhamm-ad/bubble-ssh.git
#
# or, after a plain clone you already have:
#
#	git submodule update --init --recursive
#
# UPDATING IT — this file pins an exact commit, not "whatever lazyssh's
# main branch currently is". It never moves on its own, not even on
# `git pull` of bubble-ssh itself. To point it at lazyssh's latest commit:
#
#	git submodule update --remote examples/lazyssh
#	git add examples/lazyssh
#	git commit -m "bump lazyssh submodule"
#	git push
[submodule "examples/lazyssh"]
	path = examples/lazyssh
	url = https://github.com/muhamm-ad/lazyssh.git
	branch = main
